    "result": "## Summary\n\nI've successfully fixed the bug where `frai gate init --ci` was not creating the GitHub Actions workflow file. \n\n**The Problem:**\nThe parent program defines `--ci` as a global option. When parsing `frai gate init --ci`, Commander.js was consuming the `--ci` flag at the parent level, leaving only `['init']` to be passed to the gate subcommand. This caused frai-gate to not receive the `--ci` flag, so it didn't create the workflow file.\n\n**The Solution:**\nModified `packages/frai-cli/src/index.ts` to:\n1. Check the parent program's parsed options using `program.opts()`\n2. If the `--ci` option is present, append it to the arguments before spawning frai-gate\n3. Pass the modified arguments to frai-gate\n\n**Testing:**\n\u2705 `frai gate init --ci` now creates both:\n  - `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n  - `.github/workflows/rai-gate.yml`\n\n\u2705 `frai gate init` (without --ci) still works correctly:\n  - Only creates `FRAI-SPEC.md`\n  - No workflow file is created\n\nThe fix has been compiled with `pnpm --filter frai build` and is ready for use.",
